<section class="sec" id="vision">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Why Now</div>
    <h2 data-reveal data-delay=".08">The runtime holds the line.</h2>
    <p class="lede" data-reveal data-delay=".16">When AI agents generate interfaces, the runtime does the hard work. Rust's guarantees and Makepad 2.0's declarative model give agents expressive freedom — without giving up the rules.</p>

    <p class="vision-tie" data-reveal data-delay=".3">This is the bet behind A2App and Makepad 2.0: agents describe <em>what</em> the UI should be, and a Rust-native, declarative runtime decides <em>how</em> it behaves. The model gets room to compose. The person using the app gets an interface that stays inside what the runtime allows.</p>
  </div>
</section>
